## Rendering analysis

What the `goal detail` CLI emits:
- An "**Dependencies (ASCII)**" code block — a plain-text dependency listing
  with `[ ]` / `[x]` markers and `deps:` lines (the text DAG).
- A "**Dependency Graph**" `mermaid` *source* code block (the textual Mermaid
  flowchart that a viewer like GitHub / Telegram / Mintlify can render).

What it does NOT emit:
- No PNG file path, no rendered image, no base64-encoded image in the CLI
  stdout. PNG rendering lives in `src/goal/mermaid-png.ts` and is called
  ONLY from the Telegram sender (`src/telegram/goal-sending.ts:13` imports
  `renderMermaidToPng`; `src/telegram/goal-sending.ts:800` invokes it). It
  is not wired into the CLI `goal detail` printer.

Therefore: CLI `goal detail` renders both a text DAG (ASCII) and a Mermaid
source block, but does not render a PNG. Telegram is a separate surface
that can convert the Mermaid block to a PNG, but that path was not
exercised in this run.

## Code path citations
- src/cli/program/register.goal.ts:49 — `moltbot goal detail <runId>` CLI registration.
- src/goal/format-output.ts — formatter for the text DAG / mermaid block (no PNG).
- src/goal/mermaid-png.ts:33 — `renderMermaidToPng`, only used by Telegram.
- src/telegram/goal-sending.ts:13,800 — Telegram surface invoking PNG renderer.

## Safe README wording
- "text DAG verified only" — for the CLI surface.
- "renders a task graph as both an ASCII dependency list and a Mermaid
  flowchart source block" — accurate description of CLI output.
- "Telegram surface renders the Mermaid graph as a PNG" — only safe if
  separately verified live; in this audit it was static-only.

## Unsafe README wording to avoid
- "renders a graphical PNG dependency graph in the terminal" (false for CLI).
- "renders a Mermaid diagram out of the box on every channel" (unverified).

